1: ERROR: duplicate output key `:k` in the select block — two branches deliver the same output key, and distinct keys are required (strict merge; the alternative is a silent last-write-wins). The key may be one a branch NAMES, or one a star (`*`) LIFTED out of its layer. Rename an UNSTARRED branch with `^k'` (`x{k^k2}`) — a starred segment cannot carry a rename — or select the flatten in its own block. Dropping a star re-nests what it lifted — `*` under the key the star was deleting — which resolves the collision unless another branch delivers that key too.
